@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("foo", "bar", sep=".", end="!")
+
+Unlike print, out does not pretty print containers, does not wrap or crop text, does not interpret markup or emoji codes, and does not add logging information. Output is written literally.
+
+Out does apply highlighting by default, which you can turn off with ``highlight=False``, and it accepts a basic ``style`` argument applied in the same way as print.
+
+
